IMPORT prelude

-- Platform Workers Act 2024 (Singapore) -- CPF contributions on platform earnings: s 97 and the Fourth Schedule para 4, which
-- insert s 8A and a new Fourth Schedule ("Platform worker contributions") into the Central Provident Fund Act 1953. Encoded:
-- the fixed expenses deduction and aggregate platform earnings (Fourth Schedule paras 1 to 3), Group A and Group B (paras 4, 5
-- and 8), rounding (para 9(b), (c)), the combined ceiling for a platform operator only (para 10), provisional deduction and
-- refund (para 13(1)(b) and (3)), the Group A rates in all five phase-in steps (paras 14 to 18), the Group B rates (para 19),
-- and the cap on recovery (CPF Act s 8A(5)).
--
-- Edition: the Act as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PWA2024.txt (SSO informal consolidation, version in force
-- from 4 May 2026), Fourth Schedule para 19 (the inserted CPF Fourth Schedule). The inserted Schedule has since been amended by
-- notification under CPF Act s 8A(8) (S 1026/2024 wef 1 January 2025; S 886/2025 wef 1 January 2026), so it was read against
-- ../../../central-provident-fund-act-1953/registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953.txt (version in force from 1 July 2026), Fourth
-- Schedule. The Group A and Group B rate tables are identical in the two deposits (all 40 Group A bands compared); para 10
-- (the combined ceiling) and the definitions in para 1 are taken from the CPF deposit, where they were recast by S 1026/2024.
-- The CPF deposit marks the Schedule "[Act 30 of 2024 wef 15/12/2024]", so para 14 governs relevant months from January 2025.
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0267 (Jun Hao scenario, event j041): a platform worker born in 2006 earns $2,900 in
-- March 2027 from a delivery platform; what must the operator contribute to his CPF, and what is deducted from his earnings?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: who is a platform worker (pwa-coverage.l4); any limit to citizens and permanent residents, or other exclusion,
-- made by regulations under CPF Act s 77(1), to which s 8A(1) is "subject" (not deposited); payments excluded from "platform
-- earnings" by the Minister's notification (none deposited); the mixed-transport rules of para 3(b) and (d)(ii) (the encoding
-- takes one mode of transport); the transitional months of paras 6 and 7 for a worker who opts in, and the Board's alternative
-- months (s 8A(7)(b)); 29 February birthdays (para 9(a)(ii)); the combined ceilings where the operator also pays wages or is a
-- related contributor (paras 10A to 10C); the deadlines for payment and deduction (paras 11 to 13(2)); interest (s 9); the
-- offences (s 8A(3), (5)); voluntary contributions (s 8A(4)); allocation to the CPF accounts.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Platform Workers Act 2024 -- CPF contributions on platform earnings`

§§ `CPF Fourth Schedule paras 1 to 3 -- aggregate platform earnings`

-- Para 1(1): "'aggregate platform earnings' or 'APE', for a relevant month, means the amount of platform earnings payable in
-- the relevant month less the fixed expenses deduction amounts computed in accordance with paragraph 2".
-- Para 2: the deduction "is computed as the applicable percentage of those platform earnings".
-- Para 3, table: "By using a motor vehicle other than a motorcycle" 60%; "By using a personal mobility device,
-- power-assisted bicycle or motorcycle" 35%; "On foot, by public transport or by using a bicycle (not being power-assisted)"
-- 20%. Para 3(d)(iii), for earnings not tied to tasks: "if no mode of transport is recorded by the platform operator -- 20%".
DECLARE Transport IS ONE OF
    `a motor vehicle other than a motorcycle`
    `a personal mobility device, power-assisted bicycle or motorcycle`
    `on foot, by public transport or by a bicycle that is not power-assisted`
    `no mode of transport recorded`

GIVEN mode IS A Transport
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fixed expenses percentage for` mode MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `a motor vehicle other than a motorcycle` THEN 0.6
    WHEN `a personal mobility device, power-assisted bicycle or motorcycle` THEN 0.35
    WHEN `on foot, by public transport or by a bicycle that is not power-assisted` THEN 0.2
    WHEN `no mode of transport recorded` THEN 0.2

GIVEN `platform earnings` IS A NUMBER, mode IS A Transport
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregate platform earnings` `platform earnings` mode MEANS
    `platform earnings` MINUS `platform earnings` TIMES `the fixed expenses percentage for` mode

§§ `CPF Fourth Schedule paras 4, 5 and 8 -- Group A and Group B`

-- Para 5: "Part 3 of this Schedule applies to a platform worker (called in this Schedule a Group A worker) -- (a) who was born
-- on or after 1 January 1995; or (b) who was born before 1 January 1995 and opts to be a Group A worker under paragraph 4(1)".
-- Para 4(3): the option "cannot be withdrawn". Para 8: Part 4 (Group B) applies, "Subject to paragraphs 5, 6 and 7", to a
-- worker born before a date the CPF deposit gives as "1 January 2026" (as amended by S 886/2025; the Act as enacted said
-- "1 January 1995"). Because para 8 yields to para 5, the result is the same: born in 1995 or later means Group A.
-- Birth year stands in for the date of birth, which is exact here because the cut-off is 1 January.
GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `opted to be a Group A worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Group A worker` IF
        `birth year` AT LEAST 1995
    OR  `opted to be a Group A worker`

§§ `CPF Fourth Schedule para 9 -- age and rounding`

-- Para 9(a)(i): the contributions "payable according to the age of a platform worker specified in Part 3 or 4 ... are payable
-- -- from the first day of the month following the month in which the platform worker attains that age". As in the CPF row's
-- cpf-rates-and-death.l4, the band for a month is fixed by the age in completed years at the end of the PREVIOUS month, and a
-- band "above 35" is read as an age of 36 or more on that count. INFERENCE: CPF Board practice may move a worker to the
-- "above 35" rates from the month after the 35th birthday; that reading would change only the months at a band's edge.
GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth month` IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age that sets the band for the month` `birth year` `birth month` year month MEANS
    IF `birth month` LESS THAN month
    THEN year MINUS `birth year`
    ELSE year MINUS `birth year` MINUS 1

-- Para 9(b): "the contribution payable by the platform operator is to be rounded off to the nearest dollar except, where the
-- fraction of the dollar is 50 cents, is to be regarded as a dollar"; (c): "in calculating the amount recoverable by the
-- platform operator from the platform worker's platform remuneration, a fraction of a dollar is to be ignored".
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded off to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up` x MEANS FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

§§ `CPF Fourth Schedule Part 3 -- Group A rates, paras 14 to 18`

-- Every Group A table has the same shape. APE "$50 or less": NIL and NIL. "Exceeding $50 but not exceeding $500": the operator
-- pays "an amount equal to [low rate] of APE", nothing recoverable. "Exceeding $500 but not exceeding $750": the sum of "(a)
-- [low rate] of APE; and (b) [factor] of the difference between APE and $500", of which "[factor] of the difference between
-- APE and $500" is recoverable. "Exceeding $750": "[total rate] of APE", of which "[recoverable rate] of APE" is recoverable.
-- The second column is the TOTAL the operator pays to the Fund; the third is what it may recover from the worker.
DECLARE PlatformRates HAS
    `low rate` IS A NUMBER
    `phase-in factor` IS A NUMBER
    `total rate` IS A NUMBER
    `recoverable rate` IS A NUMBER

-- Para 14: "for each relevant month following the month in which paragraph 19 of the Fourth Schedule to the Platform Workers
-- Act 2024 is commenced" (from January 2025). Bands (a) 35 or below; (b) above 35 to 45; (c) above 45 to 50; (d) above 50 to
-- 55; (e) above 55 to 60; (f) above 60 to 65; (g) above 65 to 70; (h) above 70.
-- (a) 3.5% / 0.315 / 14% of which 10.5%; (b) 3.5% / 0.345 / 15% of which 11.5%; (c) 3.5% / 0.375 / 16% of which 12.5%;
-- (d), (e) 3.5% / 0.39 / 16.5% of which 13%; (f), (g) 3.5% / 0.315 / 14% of which 10.5%; (h) 3.5% / 0.27 / 12.5% of which 9%.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PlatformRates
`the paragraph 14 rates for` age MEANS
    IF age AT MOST 35 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.035, `phase-in factor` IS 0.315, `total rate` IS 0.14, `recoverable rate` IS 0.105
    ELSE IF age AT MOST 45 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.035, `phase-in factor` IS 0.345, `total rate` IS 0.15, `recoverable rate` IS 0.115
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 50 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.035, `phase-in factor` IS 0.375, `total rate` IS 0.16, `recoverable rate` IS 0.125
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 60 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.035, `phase-in factor` IS 0.39, `total rate` IS 0.165, `recoverable rate` IS 0.13
                   ELSE IF age AT MOST 70 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.035, `phase-in factor` IS 0.315, `total rate` IS 0.14, `recoverable rate` IS 0.105
                        ELSE PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.035, `phase-in factor` IS 0.27, `total rate` IS 0.125, `recoverable rate` IS 0.09

-- Para 15: "for each relevant month starting on or after 1 January 2026".
-- (a) 7% / 0.39 / 20% of which 13%; (b) 7% / 0.42 / 21% of which 14%; (c) 7% / 0.45 / 22% of which 15%; (d), (e) 7% / 0.465 /
-- 22.5% of which 15.5%; (f) 7% / 0.375 / 19.5% of which 12.5%; (g) 7% / 0.285 / 16.5% of which 9.5%; (h) 7% / 0.165 / 12.5% of
-- which 5.5%.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PlatformRates
`the paragraph 15 rates for` age MEANS
    IF age AT MOST 35 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.07, `phase-in factor` IS 0.39, `total rate` IS 0.2, `recoverable rate` IS 0.13
    ELSE IF age AT MOST 45 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.07, `phase-in factor` IS 0.42, `total rate` IS 0.21, `recoverable rate` IS 0.14
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 50 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.07, `phase-in factor` IS 0.45, `total rate` IS 0.22, `recoverable rate` IS 0.15
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 60 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.07, `phase-in factor` IS 0.465, `total rate` IS 0.225, `recoverable rate` IS 0.155
                   ELSE IF age AT MOST 65 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.07, `phase-in factor` IS 0.375, `total rate` IS 0.195, `recoverable rate` IS 0.125
                        ELSE IF age AT MOST 70 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.07, `phase-in factor` IS 0.285, `total rate` IS 0.165, `recoverable rate` IS 0.095
                             ELSE PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.07, `phase-in factor` IS 0.165, `total rate` IS 0.125, `recoverable rate` IS 0.055

-- Para 16: "for each relevant month starting on or after 1 January 2027". THIS IS THE TABLE REQ-0267 NEEDS.
-- (a) "where the Group A worker is 35 years of age or below": 10.5% / 0.465 / "26% of APE" of which "15.5% of APE";
-- (b) 10.5% / 0.495 / 27% of which 16.5%; (c) 10.5% / 0.525 / 28% of which 17.5%; (d), (e) 10.5% / 0.54 / 28.5% of which 18%;
-- (f) 10.5% / 0.39 / 23.5% of which 13%; (g) 9% / 0.225 / 16.5% of which 7.5%; (h) 7.5% / 0.15 / 12.5% of which 5%.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PlatformRates
`the paragraph 16 rates for` age MEANS
    IF age AT MOST 35 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.105, `phase-in factor` IS 0.465, `total rate` IS 0.26, `recoverable rate` IS 0.155
    ELSE IF age AT MOST 45 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.105, `phase-in factor` IS 0.495, `total rate` IS 0.27, `recoverable rate` IS 0.165
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 50 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.105, `phase-in factor` IS 0.525, `total rate` IS 0.28, `recoverable rate` IS 0.175
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 60 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.105, `phase-in factor` IS 0.54, `total rate` IS 0.285, `recoverable rate` IS 0.18
                   ELSE IF age AT MOST 65 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.105, `phase-in factor` IS 0.39, `total rate` IS 0.235, `recoverable rate` IS 0.13
                        ELSE IF age AT MOST 70 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.09, `phase-in factor` IS 0.225, `total rate` IS 0.165, `recoverable rate` IS 0.075
                             ELSE PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.075, `phase-in factor` IS 0.15, `total rate` IS 0.125, `recoverable rate` IS 0.05

-- Para 17: "for each relevant month starting on or after 1 January 2028".
-- (a) 14% / 0.54 / 32% of which 18%; (b) 14% / 0.57 / 33% of which 19%; (c), (d), (e) 14% / 0.6 / 34% of which 20%;
-- (f) 13% / 0.39 / 26% of which 13%; (g) 9% / 0.225 / 16.5% of which 7.5%; (h) 7.5% / 0.15 / 12.5% of which 5%.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PlatformRates
`the paragraph 17 rates for` age MEANS
    IF age AT MOST 35 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.14, `phase-in factor` IS 0.54, `total rate` IS 0.32, `recoverable rate` IS 0.18
    ELSE IF age AT MOST 45 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.14, `phase-in factor` IS 0.57, `total rate` IS 0.33, `recoverable rate` IS 0.19
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 60 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.14, `phase-in factor` IS 0.6, `total rate` IS 0.34, `recoverable rate` IS 0.2
              ELSE IF age AT MOST 65 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.13, `phase-in factor` IS 0.39, `total rate` IS 0.26, `recoverable rate` IS 0.13
                   ELSE IF age AT MOST 70 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.09, `phase-in factor` IS 0.225, `total rate` IS 0.165, `recoverable rate` IS 0.075
                        ELSE PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.075, `phase-in factor` IS 0.15, `total rate` IS 0.125, `recoverable rate` IS 0.05

-- Para 18: "for each relevant month starting on or after 1 January 2029" -- the end of the phase-in, equal to the employee
-- rates of the CPF First Schedule para 1 from 1 January 2026.
-- (a) to (e) 17% / 0.6 / 37% of which 20%; (f) 13% / 0.39 / 26% of which 13%; (g) 9% / 0.225 / 16.5% of which 7.5%;
-- (h) 7.5% / 0.15 / 12.5% of which 5%.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PlatformRates
`the paragraph 18 rates for` age MEANS
    IF age AT MOST 60 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.17, `phase-in factor` IS 0.6, `total rate` IS 0.37, `recoverable rate` IS 0.2
    ELSE IF age AT MOST 65 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.13, `phase-in factor` IS 0.39, `total rate` IS 0.26, `recoverable rate` IS 0.13
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 70 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.09, `phase-in factor` IS 0.225, `total rate` IS 0.165, `recoverable rate` IS 0.075
              ELSE PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0.075, `phase-in factor` IS 0.15, `total rate` IS 0.125, `recoverable rate` IS 0.05

-- Which paragraph governs a relevant month. The Schedule commenced on 15 December 2024, so para 14 starts with January 2025;
-- a month before 2025 has no Group A table (the caller gets nothing payable, below).
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PlatformRates
`the Group A rates for` age year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2029 THEN `the paragraph 18 rates for` age
    ELSE IF year EQUALS 2028 THEN `the paragraph 17 rates for` age
         ELSE IF year EQUALS 2027 THEN `the paragraph 16 rates for` age
              ELSE IF year EQUALS 2026 THEN `the paragraph 15 rates for` age
                   ELSE `the paragraph 14 rates for` age

§§ `CPF Fourth Schedule Part 4 -- Group B rates, para 19`

-- Para 19: one table, no phase-in. APE "$500 or less": NIL. "Exceeding $500 but not exceeding $750": "an amount equal to
-- [factor] of the difference between APE and $500". "Exceeding $750": "an amount equal to [rate] of APE". The single column is
-- headed "Contributions payable by platform operator for relevant month and amount recoverable": the WHOLE contribution may be
-- recovered from the worker. (a) 35 or below: 0.24 / 8%; (b) above 35 to 45: 0.27 / 9%; (c) above 45 to 50: 0.3 / 10%;
-- (d) above 50: 0.315 / 10.5%.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PlatformRates
`the Group B rates for` age MEANS
    IF age AT MOST 35 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0, `phase-in factor` IS 0.24, `total rate` IS 0.08, `recoverable rate` IS 0.08
    ELSE IF age AT MOST 45 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0, `phase-in factor` IS 0.27, `total rate` IS 0.09, `recoverable rate` IS 0.09
         ELSE IF age AT MOST 50 THEN PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0, `phase-in factor` IS 0.3, `total rate` IS 0.1, `recoverable rate` IS 0.1
              ELSE PlatformRates WITH `low rate` IS 0, `phase-in factor` IS 0.315, `total rate` IS 0.105, `recoverable rate` IS 0.105

GIVEN `group A` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PlatformRates
`the platform rates for` `group A` age year MEANS
    IF `group A` THEN `the Group A rates for` age year ELSE `the Group B rates for` age

§§ `The month's contribution and recoverable amount`

-- With a Group B worker the low rate is 0, so the "$50 to $500" step gives nil, as para 19 says for "$500 or less".
GIVEN `group A` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, ape IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the platform contribution before rounding` `group A` age year ape MEANS
    IF year LESS THAN 2025 OR ape AT MOST 50 THEN 0
    ELSE IF ape AT MOST 500 THEN ape TIMES (`the platform rates for` `group A` age year)'s `low rate`
         ELSE IF ape AT MOST 750
              THEN ape TIMES (`the platform rates for` `group A` age year)'s `low rate`
                   PLUS (ape MINUS 500) TIMES (`the platform rates for` `group A` age year)'s `phase-in factor`
              ELSE ape TIMES (`the platform rates for` `group A` age year)'s `total rate`

GIVEN `group A` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, ape IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the recoverable amount before rounding` `group A` age year ape MEANS
    IF year LESS THAN 2025 OR ape AT MOST 500 THEN 0
    ELSE IF ape AT MOST 750 THEN (ape MINUS 500) TIMES (`the platform rates for` `group A` age year)'s `phase-in factor`
         ELSE ape TIMES (`the platform rates for` `group A` age year)'s `recoverable rate`

-- What the platform operator must pay to the Fund for the month (CPF Act s 8A(1)), rounded under para 9(b).
GIVEN `group A` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, ape IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the platform operator's contribution` `group A` age year ape MEANS
    `rounded off to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up` (`the platform contribution before rounding` `group A` age year ape)

-- What the operator may deduct from the worker's platform remuneration (s 8A(2)), fractions ignored under para 9(c).
GIVEN `group A` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, ape IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable from the platform worker` `group A` age year ape MEANS
    FLOOR (`the recoverable amount before rounding` `group A` age year ape)

-- What the operator bears itself: the contribution less what it may recover.
GIVEN `group A` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, ape IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the platform operator's own share` `group A` age year ape MEANS
    `the platform operator's contribution` `group A` age year ape MINUS `the amount recoverable from the platform worker` `group A` age year ape

§§ `CPF Fourth Schedule para 10 -- the combined ceiling (platform operator only)`

-- Para 10 (as recast by S 1026/2024): "no contribution is payable by a platform operator on any part of a platform worker's
-- total aggregate platform earnings for any year ... which is in excess of the applicable amount". "Applicable amount" (First
-- Schedule para 5(da)): "$102,000". INFERENCE: the encoding applies the ceiling by cutting down the month's APE before the
-- rates are applied, taking the APE of earlier months in the year from the same operator as given.
GIVEN ape IS A NUMBER, `APE earlier in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the APE within the combined ceiling` ape `APE earlier in the year` MEANS
    IF `APE earlier in the year` AT LEAST 102000 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `APE earlier in the year` PLUS ape GREATER THAN 102000 THEN 102000 MINUS `APE earlier in the year`
         ELSE ape

§§ `CPF Fourth Schedule para 13(1)(b) and (3) -- provisional deduction and refund`

-- Para 13(1): the operator "may deduct the recoverable amount in respect of each platform earning at the rate applicable ...
-- (a) corresponding to the amount of the platform worker's aggregate platform earnings for the relevant month computed as of
-- the time that deduction is made; or (b) as if the platform worker's aggregate platform earnings for the relevant month
-- exceeds $750." (3): it "must refund to the platform worker any amount deducted in excess of the recoverable amount applicable
-- to the platform worker's actual aggregate platform earnings for the relevant month not later than 14 days after the end of
-- the relevant month". INFERENCE: the para 13(1)(b) deduction is the "exceeding $750" recoverable rate on the APE, fractions
-- ignored.
GIVEN `group A` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, ape IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction as if APE exceeded 750` `group A` age year ape MEANS
    IF year LESS THAN 2025 THEN 0
    ELSE FLOOR (ape TIMES (`the platform rates for` `group A` age year)'s `recoverable rate`)

GIVEN `group A` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER, ape IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund due after a provisional deduction` `group A` age year ape MEANS
    `the deduction as if APE exceeded 750` `group A` age year ape MINUS `the amount recoverable from the platform worker` `group A` age year ape

§§ `CPF Act s 8A(5) -- no recovery beyond the recoverable amount`

-- s 8A(5): "a platform operator is not entitled to recover in any way from a platform worker in respect of contributions
-- payable under this Act any sum in excess of the total amount that the platform operator is permitted to recover under
-- subsection (2) ... and any platform operator that recovers or attempts to recover any greater sum shall be guilty of an
-- offence."
GIVEN `amount recovered` IS A NUMBER, `amount recoverable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recovery is within section 8A(5)` IF `amount recovered` AT MOST `amount recoverable`
